WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.024 --> 00:00:03.176
Five bytes enter the download path.

2
00:00:03.176 --> 00:00:06.865
The careful courier, File Client, brings back exactly five.

3
00:00:06.865 --> 00:00:09.879
Now Remote Workspace handles the very same file.

4
00:01:06.522 --> 00:01:09.058
Remote Workspace returns eleven bytes.

5
00:01:09.058 --> 00:01:13.062
Three original bytes put on replacement-character costumes.

6
00:01:13.062 --> 00:01:14.596
The parcel got bigger.

7
00:01:14.596 --> 00:01:16.532
The information got smaller.

8
00:01:18.361 --> 00:01:21.315
The direct File Client preserves all five bytes.

9
00:01:21.315 --> 00:01:25.624
Remote Workspace silently changes them, and reports the changed size.

10
00:01:25.624 --> 00:01:28.516
This defect was independently confirmed twice.
